---
import Page from '../../layouts/Page.astro';
import { routes } from '../../i18n/routes';
---

<Page
  route="mobilis"
  title="Mobilis: control your phone by voice"
  heading="Mobilis: control your whole phone by voice"
  description="A voice assistant that operates your whole phone and answers out loud, for people with tetraplegia and anyone who cannot handle their phone."
  lead="You speak, Mobilis acts on the phone, then answers out loud. No need to hold the device or look at the screen."
>
  <h2>Who it is for</h2>
  <p>
    Mobilis is designed first for people living with a spinal cord injury, especially tetraplegia. It
    also serves anyone who cannot handle their phone: other motor impairments, older people, situations
    where your hands are not free.
  </p>

  <h2>How it works</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>You start listening and say what you need in your own words, with no commands to memorise.</li>
    <li>Mobilis understands the request and acts on the phone: open an app, write, call, look something up.</li>
    <li>Mobilis answers out loud and tells you what it did.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>How it differs from built-in voice commands</h2>
  <p>
    Phones already offer free voice commands. They run fixed commands that must be said in a precise way.
    Mobilis understands a request phrased freely and gives you the information out loud, instead of only
    running an action.
  </p>

  <h2>Which phones</h2>
  <p>
    Mobilis is in testing on Android. Other systems will follow. iPhone will come last: iOS currently
    restricts the level of phone control Mobilis needs.
  </p>

  <h2>Your data</h2>
  <p>
    Most of your data stays stored on your phone. To understand your requests, Mobilis currently relies
    on a language model from an external provider, so your requests pass through that service. We are
    working on moving to a securely hosted model under our control. We only collect the data the service
    needs, and we anonymise or pseudonymise it whenever possible.
  </p>
  <p>
    Mobilis is an accessibility tool. It is not a medical device and does not replace any care or
    rehabilitation.
  </p>

  <h2>Where Mobilis stands</h2>
  <p>
    The app works and is in testing. We are looking for testers to improve it with the people who will
    use it every day.
  </p>
  <div class="actions">
    <a class="button" href={routes.tester.en}>Become a tester</a>
  </div>
</Page>
